## English

### 1. What is granted

You are granted permission to install and use Atreus on the machines you use,
personally and free of charge. This permission is revocable, non-exclusive and
non-transferable.

### 2. What is not granted

Without written permission from the copyright holder, you may not:

  a) redistribute Atreus, in whole or in part, free or for a fee, on its own or
     inside another product;
  b) publish Atreus, or any derivative work, under another name, another brand
     or someone else's authorship;
  c) sell, rent, sublicense or lend Atreus;
  d) remove or alter the copyright, authorship or licence notices.

The code being readable does not imply permission: Electron hands the
JavaScript to the user because of how it works, not because any right over it
is given away.

### 3. What you may do with the code

You may read the code, study it and modify your own copy for your own personal
use. What you may not do is distribute the result.

### 4. Third-party content

Atreus shows content that is not its own — guides, maps, achievement lists,
cover art and mod catalogues — taken from public sources and always linked back
to where it came from. That content belongs to whoever wrote or published it
and is not covered by this licence. Atreus neither hosts nor republishes it.

Atreus bundles third-party open-source software, each piece under its own
licence. Those licences continue to apply to their respective components.

### 5. No warranty

Atreus is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied.
The copyright holder is not liable for any damage arising from its use.

This matters especially for one particular feature: Atreus can write
achievements to your Steam account if you ask it to. That write is your
responsibility, the application warns you before doing it, and there is no way
to fully undo what remains on your public profile.

### 6. End of the licence

This permission terminates automatically if you breach any of its terms.
